# The ONE schedule (backend-etl map, ruling 1). Two readers, one file:
#   - the compose `worker` runs supercronic over it (mounted at /etc/crontab
#     by deploy/docker-compose.yml);
#   - deploy/cloudrun/install_schedule.py turns each line into a Cloud
#     Scheduler entry that runs the Cloud Run Job with `manage.py <task>`.
# Every line must be exactly `<5-field cron> python manage.py <task>`:
# install_schedule.py refuses any other shape, and supercronic runs the line
# as written from /app, so a bare `manage.py` (no interpreter) would not run.
# Times are UTC (the container clock and Cloud Scheduler's default).
#
# Tickets 03-07 add their own lines below this one.

# Ticket 01: records that the scheduler fires. Nothing else.
*/30 * * * * python manage.py heartbeat

# Ticket 03: pg_dump of the database to the operator household's Drive
# (LEGION backups/<date>/), 90 daily kept. 03:00 UTC.
0 3 * * * python manage.py backup_nightly

# Ticket 04: Canvas coursework into events (kind=task), for every household
# that has handed over a Canvas session. Every half hour.
*/30 * * * * python manage.py canvas_poll

# Ticket 06: bank statements dropped in the household's Drive statements folder,
# read and committed through the section 4 gate. Every six hours.
0 */6 * * * python manage.py drive_statements

# ADR 0057: the bank's own transaction feed (Plaid) into the ledger, for every
# household with a bank connected. Every three hours, at :30, so it never lands on
# drive_statements' hour (that one runs every six, on the hour).
30 */3 * * * python manage.py plaid_sync

# ai-upgrade ticket 02: the daily brief at 05:00 HOUSEHOLD-LOCAL time. This file
# is UTC (install_schedule.py passes no --time-zone), so it runs every hour and
# the command builds only for a household whose local clock has reached 05:00
# and has no brief yet today: right through DST and for every household's zone.
0 * * * * python manage.py morning_brief

# web-revamp ticket 15: Web Push - list changes, event reminders and the
# morning list, deduped in public.push_sent. Every five minutes. With the
# VAPID_* keys unset it says push is off and sends nothing.
*/5 * * * * python manage.py push_dispatch

# recruiter-demo ticket 13: each recruiter visit has its own copy of the demo
# household; delete the copies (and their visitors and tokens) whose visit has
# ended. Hourly at :20, clear of push_dispatch's and morning_brief's minutes.
20 * * * * python manage.py prune_demo_visitors

# claude-session ticket 03 (ADR 0067): Claude session tasks, their files and
# session rows older than 30 days deleted. Daily, 03:30 UTC (after the backup).
30 3 * * * python manage.py claude_session_prune

# household-finance ticket 01 (ADR 0073): one balance snapshot a day for each
# Plaid-linked household account, from the balances plaid_sync stored. 21:45
# UTC, fifteen minutes after that hour's plaid_sync (30 */3).
45 21 * * * python manage.py finance_snapshots

# household-finance ticket 03 (ADR 0073): the day's USD/SGD rate, stored as
# int micros. 17:00 UTC, after the ECB publishes its daily reference rates.
0 17 * * * python manage.py fx_rates

# memory-and-vault ticket 03 (ADR 0075): finished conversation records (phone, web) distilled
# into each member's private memories on the household's Gemini key. Hourly at :40, clear of
# the other jobs' minutes. With LEGION_GEMINI_KEY unset it says so and marks nothing.
40 * * * * python manage.py consolidate_memories
